B.Ef=new A.c9("Epilepsy vs PNES","Lateral tongue bite strongly favors a generalized tonic-clonic epileptic seizure over PNES.")
B.E5=new A.c9("Epilepsy vs PNES","Forced or resisted eye closure during the event favors PNES \u2014 eyes are open in the great majority of epileptic seizures.")
B.Ei=new A.c9("Epilepsy vs PNES","Todd's paralysis strongly supports a focal epileptic seizure and is rarely, if ever, seen in PNES.")
B.Ee=new A.c9("Epilepsy vs PNES","Asynchronous, out-of-phase limb thrashing favors PNES; epileptic clonic activity is typically synchronous and rhythmic.")
B.Eo=new A.c9("Epilepsy vs PNES","Immediate, full recovery without postictal confusion argues against a generalized epileptic seizure.")
B.En=new A.c9("Epilepsy vs PNES","A normal post-ictal serum prolactin after a witnessed convulsive event favors PNES; a rise at 10-20 minutes favors epilepsy.")
B.Eb=new A.c9("Epilepsy vs PNES","PNES and epilepsy frequently coexist in the same patient \u2014 diagnosing one does not exclude the other.")
B.Eg=new A.c9("Epilepsy vs PNES","Events lasting many minutes with preserved oxygenation are more typical of PNES; most epileptic seizures self-terminate within 1-2 minutes.")
B.El=new A.c9("Localization","D\xe9j\xe0 vu, epigastric rising, and oroalimentary automatisms usually suggest temporal lobe onset.")
B.E6=new A.c9("Localization","The figure-of-4 sign and fencing (M2e) posture lateralize to a supplementary motor area (frontal) seizure, contralateral to the extended arm.")
B.Ej=new A.c9("Localization","Brief, frequent, clustered nocturnal seizures with rapid recovery point toward a frontal lobe origin.")
B.Er=new A.c9("Localization","Elementary visual hallucinations (flashing lights) suggest occipital onset; slower, spreading, colored scintillations suggest migraine instead.")
B.Ep=new A.c9("Localization","Painful unilateral paresthesia with dysautonomia and a choking sensation should raise suspicion for insular onset.")
B.Ed=new A.c9("Localization","Frontal lobe seizures are frequently MRI-negative even when focal cortical dysplasia is the underlying cause.")
B.Eh=new A.c9("Syndromes","Gelastic seizures suggest a hypothalamic hamartoma, especially when accompanied by precocious puberty in a child.")
B.E8=new A.c9("Syndromes","Ask every adolescent with early-morning myoclonic jerks about juvenile myoclonic epilepsy before labeling episodes as clumsiness.")
B.Ea=new A.c9("Syndromes","Infantile spasms with developmental regression are a pediatric neurologic emergency requiring urgent EEG (hypsarrhythmia) and treatment.")
B.E7=new A.c9("Syndromes","Catamenial epilepsy is best confirmed with a seizure diary correlated against a menstrual calendar, not by history alone.")
B.Et=new A.c9("Syndromes","Reflex epilepsies (photosensitive, reading, musicogenic, hot water, startle) share a stereotyped trigger-to-seizure relationship \u2014 ask specifically about triggers.")
B.Ec=new A.c9("Mimics","Convulsive syncope is the single most commonly misdiagnosed seizure mimic in adults \u2014 look for a presyncopal prodrome and rapid full recovery.")
B.Ek=new A.c9("Mimics","Brief myoclonic jerks during a faint (anoxic myoclonus) do not make an event epileptic.")
B.Es=new A.c9("Mimics","Always check a bedside glucose during the acute evaluation of any transient event \u2014 hypoglycemia is a readily reversible mimic.")
B.E9=new A.c9("Mimics","Migraine with aura evolves more slowly (minutes) than an epileptic aura (seconds) and is usually followed by headache.")
B.Eq=new A.c9("Investigations","A single normal interictal EEG does not exclude epilepsy \u2014 sensitivity rises with sleep-deprived and repeated recordings.")
B.Eu=new A.c9("Investigations","Video-EEG monitoring capturing a typical habitual event remains the diagnostic gold standard when the differential is unclear.")
B.Em=new A.c9("Investigations","Elevated CK and a transient venous lactate rise support a recent convulsive epileptic seizure.")
